    "created_at": "2023-01-13T02:39:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-01-13T02:39:40Z",
    "body": "I want to repeat what @noamr said on internal chat, because I think it's really insightful:\r\n\r\n> I think what's confusing about nested is that it implies a hierarchical relationship, and the relationship between the container and its navigable is one of box->cargo rather than of parent->child, therefore content/attached/containee, something that implies a different \"type\" of thing\r\n\r\nThis makes me feel more confident that renaming is a good idea. I'm ambivalent between \"content navigable\" and \"navigable\".\r\n\r\n> Historically we called them \"nested\"\r\n\r\nThis isn't actually true, it appears. E.g. https://html.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/c9e804f04d03a0658bfa689cb0f368a4d2e37936/#nested-browsing-context uses \"nested\" for the property and \"child\" for the predicate / tree relationship.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
